scriptunit-edit 3
----------

var d = 5

----------
expect unit 3 is edited back so unit 4 finishes
----------

| unit | uses | this step | because | holds after |
|------|------|-----------|---------|-------------|
| 1 | - | untouched | unit 5 revives `a` and needs nothing it held | `a` taken |
| 2 | takes `a` (1) | untouched | uses nothing that changed | `b` = [1] |
| 3 | - | recompiles, runs | edited | `d` = 5 |
| 4 | reads `d` (3) | reruns | reads `d` from unit 3 | `q` = 20 |
| 5 | reads `q` (4), revives `a` (1) | reruns | reads `q` from unit 4, which finished | `e` = 21 |
| 6 | takes `a` (1) | reruns | takes `a` after unit 5, which revives it again | `c` = [2] |

----------
engine
----------

| unit | this step | note |
|------|-----------|------|
| 1 | reruns | unit 5 reads from unit 4, which may return early, so its revive may not happen and counts as an update |
| 2 | reruns | it took `a`, which unit 1 builds again |
